From 574cc9e78a5194cafd7988f60c2e71382cd226c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LECH OS <dev@lech-os.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Google zone settings of LECH OS: Slovak texts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The settings of the sandboxed Google Play (Android Auto permissions,
Play services, notifications of the compatibility layer) were English only
(Pixel 9, 15. 11. 2026). All texts get a Slovak translation; the screen is
called "Zóna Google" as in the settings of LECH OS (English: Google zone).
---
 res/values-sk/strings.xml | 168 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 res/values/strings.xml    |   8 +-
 2 files changed, 172 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 res/values-sk/strings.xml

diff --git a/res/values-sk/strings.xml b/res/values-sk/strings.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..15c60ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values-sk/strings.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
